## What this track proposes

The track draws 19 color pictures for Storytime Level 2 family words. Eighteen new rows use the Storytime Muse color path and the frozen Sonnet judge at card size. The family row reuses the color print of the card track. The track delivers 1500 x 1500 PNG files named l2-w0N-card-<word>-v1.png to the handoff folder, with manifest.json, MANIFEST.txt (SHA-256), and a contact sheet. The work stays inside the remaining 0.86 USD of the 1.60 USD card limit and reports one status line to the PM by 2026-11-10.

## How the current system works, per this spec

The current system has the Storytime Muse path in scripts/storytime-muse.mjs and one guard module, scripts/storytime-muse-guards.mjs. That module owns CARD_RUN: cap 1.60 USD, start 2026-11-06, 3 tries, and the card Muse folder. It classifies each spec outDir and checks spend and tries before each provider call. scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs builds judge batches from a spec folder, and it has a --cards mode. src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts holds writeMuseDelivery for list rows with color and line prints, and deliverMuseCover for one cover entry. Eighteen of the 19 words are not rows of list v7; the family word is a card row.

