## Findings

- F1 [Blocker] spec.md Delivery (deliverMuseColorSet): The specification names the entry fields rowId, version, colorPrint, reviews, and notes. It does not give the StorytimeJob values that assembleManifest needs: week, directory, bookKind, page, text, use, and size. rowCaptureJob derives them from a PictureListRow (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:3639). coverJob hard-codes the cover values (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:548). The 18 new ids are not list rows. Rationale: the plan leaves a manifest schema choice to the implementer, and no FR-5 test pins the values, so a wrong manifest can pass every gate.
- F2 [Nit] spec.md FR-12 Wording and Overview: The second sentence of FR-12 permits the word "approved" only in the PM quotation and where it names card pictures. The Overview and the Decisions section write "the approved Storytime Muse path". Rationale: a wording rule that the specification itself breaks can make the checker report a false finding. The meaning does not change.
- F3 [Nit] spec.md Judge batch input: The sentence "the cost file is the card cost file named by the spec outDir" is unclear, because the judge batch reads costs.tsv and writes no cost file. Rationale: the implementer can read it as a new write. The stated behavior is the same as --cards.

